# capacitor / mobile
# android/ and ios/ are BOTH tracked - they carry hand-edited native files
# that `cap add` alone wouldn't reproduce (android: AndroidManifest camera/mic
# perms; ios: Info.plist usage strings + export-compliance key). Each has its
# own generated .gitignore inside the directory that already excludes the
# build output, Pods/DerivedData/xcuserdata, copied web assets, and the
# generated capacitor.config.json / config.xml. The iOS project is scaffolded
# on Linux and built on a Mac (Codemagic) - no Mac needed to keep it in sync.

# e2e (Playwright) - artefacts + the throwaway homeserver's runtime state
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/.last-run.json
test/coverage/

# misc
.cache/
.turbo/
.aider*

# self-hosted F-Droid repo: config.yml holds the repo signing keystore
# password in plaintext, and repo/ is generated (APK + regenerated indices)
# - never commit secrets or regenerable binaries. Lives only on the server
# that serves jorkonvo.com/fdroid/ (see site/README.md).
site/fdroid/

# self-hosted apt repo: dists/+pool/ are fully regenerated per release by
# packaging/linux/apt/build-repo.sh (which bundles a .deb release asset -
# a 100+ MB binary that does not belong in git history). Only the exported
# public signing key is tracked. Lives only on the server that serves
# jorkonvo.com/apt/ (see site/README.md).
site/apt/dists/
site/apt/pool/
